# AI & Architecture Guidelines (.antigravityrules)

These rules are strictly enforced to maintain a clean codebase, lower token usage, and simplify agent integration.

## UI Components
- **Line Limit**: Any single React component file (in `components/`) must not exceed 250 lines of code. If a component exceeds this threshold, it must be decomposed into smaller sub-components or custom hooks.
- **Pure Markup**: Focus on JSX and presentation. Avoid bloating components with large static data, configuration objects, or extensive business logic.

## Separation of Concerns
- **UI Components**: Must reside in the `components/` directory.
- **Business Logic & APIs**: Must reside in the `lib/` directory.
- **Global TypeScript Types**: Must reside in the `types/` directory.
- **Data & Translations**: Constants and rich-text configurations must reside in `utils/` or dedicated data files in `lib/`.

## Lightweight Routes
- Files inside the `app/` directory (Next.js Page Router) must only serve as thin entrypoints/wrappers. 
- Avoid placing direct styling, nested grids, complex UI elements, or inline event handlers in `app/**/page.tsx` or `app/**/layout.tsx`. Delegate these to page components under `components/`.

## Workflow
- **Planning First**: Before starting any non-trivial modifications or feature integrations, the agent must create or update an `implementation_plan.md` in the workspace context.
